## 2. Architecture at a glance

Two entry points do most of the work:

- **`index.php`** - the whole UI shell. Emits `penumbra_vars` (server state -> JS), the theme
  registry, the client-error telemetry installer, and the system-notice banner, then loads
  `js/main.js`.
- **`js/main.js`** (~5.5 MB, 99k lines, one `$(document).ready` closure) - the entire browser
  client: rendering, pivot, search, snippets, dialogs, auditor. It is ~85% of the eager
  `<script src>` payload, parsed on every page whether or not the user ever draws a chart.

Everything else clusters around those:

