**Navigation model (2026-08-19):** the bottom-right avatar popover in the footer status bar is
the personal anchor on *every* surface (report view, home, dev mode, admin pages) - the bar is
always visible now (only `?embed=` views hide it), and the popover carries identity (the sticky
header has no "Signed in as" chip and no Home entry - the Penumbra brand mark IS the way home).
The sticky admin header is the admin area's own nav; the whole family shares ONE theme chain
(`?theme` > the home screen's settings-panel pick > global pref - analytics_all's page-local
picker is gone). Doors into the area: the "Admin tools" split buttons (home dock + the popover footers) land on
the Repository - the area's front door - while their chevron half opens a registry-driven menu
to jump straight to any specific tool. The console is a single-report control center and carries no global
nav: its repository toolbar button was removed; `Ctrl+O` still opens the repository *lightbox*
in-context (all triggers route through `window.penumbraOpenRepo()` in main.js, which no-ops for
non-global-admins exactly like the old hidden button did). On the repository page, Escape never
navigates or toggles a console - it only closes things (search, popovers, dialogs).

**The scheduler runs every 5 minutes** via the Windows Scheduled Task **`PENUMBRA Schedule
Runner`** (on oitras; recorded 2026-08-20) invoking `php.exe schedule_runner.php`. Overlap is
prevented both by the task's "don't start a new instance" policy **and** by an atomic claim in
the runner (see Landmines).

**Scheduler tab shape (2026-08-31).** Two columns: a narrow **rail** (runner control card, the
report's events list, the add row) and a wide **config panel**. The event **type is chosen in the
rail** - `#schedNewEventType` sits beside `#addNewTaskBtn` (labelled **+ Configure** since 2026-09-23) - and it hands it to
`openSchedulerForm(null, type)`, which appends a **draft card** to the list (dashed rail, `Draft`
pill, `.sched-task-draft`) and opens the form on it. The draft is DOM-only; nothing is written
until Save, so Cancel, Refresh and F5 all simply lose it. Consequences worth knowing:

- The config panel has **no Event Type dropdown**. `#schedEventType` still exists as the form's
  type field (~15 read sites, the `change` handler, and the unsaved-changes baseline all depend
  on it) but its `.sched-row` is `display:none`. `#schedTypeHeader` is the one-line replacement -
  event name plus `Draft`/`Saved event` - written by `applyTaskTypeUI` and `setEventTypeLocked`,
  so it cannot drift from the field.
- The action bar's **left slot is Delete OR Cancel, never both**: Delete for a saved event,
  Cancel for an unsaved draft. Cancel and the rail's Refresh both call `resetSchedulerView()`.
- **Everything that leaves an open event now warns identically** (`confirmLeaveScheduler()`):
  tab switch, closing the admin console, clicking another event, adding a second draft, Cancel,
  and - new as of this change - Refresh, which used to bin unsaved edits silently.
- Two ordering rules govern this form; both are in Landmines. The type is applied in a **second
  pass after** the New-Mode reset, and `_schedDraftType` must be nulled **before** any
  `loadSchedulerTaskList()` intended to dismiss the draft.
- Type wording is one vocabulary in three places - the rail `<option>` text, `SCHED_TYPE_LABELS`
